{"uid":"19d23c695c9c82a5","name":"test_a_cure_diff_that_touches_the_cited_path_leaves_the_record_pending","fullName":"tests.test_cure_invalidates#test_a_cure_diff_that_touches_the_cited_path_leaves_the_record_pending","historyId":"43e6d28a5db01c986a4c0163070e42ae","time":{"start":1791867138025,"stop":1791867138146,"duration":121},"description":"Cure-01-06 (PRD B rulings 3/4 and B.4, task 008, F06) rewrites this\n    node IN PLACE (zero fast-tier headroom -- one collected item, same as\n    before this task) to loop over an ASCII cited path (this test's own\n    original subject) and a Unicode one git's own `--name-only`\n    display-quotes (`\"docs/r\\303\\251sultats.md\"` for\n    `docs/résultats.md`) instead of adding a sibling test. Before this\n    task `_workspace_diff_paths` read that quoted rendering, which never\n    appears as a substring of the record's own unquoted `successCriteria`\n    text, so a cure that actually committed the cited Unicode path still\n    looked \"untouched\" here and un-reopened the record over evidence that\n    had in fact moved; the fix reads `-z`, NUL-delimited output instead, so\n    the reported path matches the criteria's own text again and both\n    iterations land on the same `pending` outcome.\n    ","descriptionHtml":"<p>Cure-01-06 (PRD B rulings 3/4 and B.4, task 008, F06) rewrites this<br />\nnode IN PLACE (zero fast-tier headroom -- one collected item, same as<br />\nbefore this task) to loop over an ASCII cited path (this test's own<br />\noriginal subject) and a Unicode one git's own <code>--name-only</code><br />\ndisplay-quotes (<code>&quot;docs/r\\303\\251sultats.md&quot;</code> for<br />\n<code>docs/résultats.md</code>) instead of adding a sibling test. Before this<br />\ntask <code>_workspace_diff_paths</code> read that quoted rendering, which never<br />\nappears as a substring of the record's own unquoted <code>successCriteria</code><br />\ntext, so a cure that actually committed the cited Unicode path still<b